{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>לֵאמֹר כִּי יְדַבֵּר אֲלֵיכֶם וְגוֹ׳.</b> The reason He said <b>לֵאמֹר</b> is that He gave them permission to say that it is by the word of HaShem that they perform the signs, for without this it would be forbidden for them to convey this matter even if they were asked. As they said, of blessed memory (Yoma 4a), that it is in the category of 'do not say' until He says to him לֵאמֹר — and specifically if Pharaoh asks or if they themselves wish to tell him; but there is no obligation in the matter until He says לֵאמֹר — one matter is optional and one obligatory." "Further, it intends according to their words, of blessed memory (Torat Kohanim, introduction), that wherever it is said 'to Moses and to Aaron' it means only to Moses, that he should say it to Aaron. And this is what he himself hinted at by saying <b>לֵאמֹר</b> — meaning, that what you see written, ״אֶל מֹשֶׁה וְאֶל אַהֲרֹן״, does not mean that the speech was to both of them, but rather ״לֵאמֹר״ means: to Moses, that he should say it to Aaron. And the reason He equated them in the speech is because they are equal in this commandment, for Aaron will speak to Pharaoh, as we wrote above." "<b>פַּרְעֹה לֵאמֹר תְּנוּ וְגוֹ׳.</b> The intent of His saying <b>לֵאמֹר</b> is that they should not need to wait until Pharaoh says explicitly, ״תְּנוּ לָכֶם מוֹפֵת״, and only then perform what is stated in the matter; rather, any statement whose intent is that he requires a sign or a portent, or that you see he is skeptical about the matter and denies it, saying ״מִי יֹאמַר כְּדִבְרֵיכֶם״ — even though he did not say ״תְּנוּ״ and so forth, even so, say to Aaron, ״קַח מַטְּךָ״ and so forth."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The phrase בַּל תֹּאמַר ('do not say') echoes the language of the Gemara's exegesis of לֵאמֹר in Yoma 4a, read here as a prohibition against speaking without divine authorization."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:33.408998491Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}